  "verbalization": "Pramipexole is implicated in the pathogenesis of Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome through a series of indirect pathways involving hereditary late-onset Parkinson disease. The evidence suggests that Pramipexole may act as a secondary mediator in the development of this syndrome, as it is associated with indications for hereditary late-onset Parkinson disease, which in turn is linked to the syndrome through pharmacological and pathophysiological mechanisms. The shared indication with Pimavanserin and Istradefylline further supports a potential role in the syndrome, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The presence of a consistent score across multiple paths indicates a plausible, though not yet fully elucidated, relationship between Pramipexole and the syndrome. The mechanisms likely involve neurodegenerative processes, though the specific pathways remain to be determined. The integration of these pathways highlights the need for further investigation into the role of Pramipexole in the pathogenesis of this condition.",
